# Data Layer

## Data Source

All data is bundled as JSON files in `assets/`. There are no runtime API calls.

- Quran Arabic (KFGQPC PUA glyphs): `assets/quran/KFGQPCQuranMushaf_smart_v8.json`
- Quran Arabic (standard Uthmanic): `assets/quran/ar/{surahId}.json` — used for tajweed coloring and Google Fonts display. Generated by `tools/build_arabic_and_chapters.dart`.
- Quran translations: `assets/quran/en.clearquran/{surahId}.json`
- Surah metadata: `assets/quran/surah_metadata.json` (revelation type, order, juz ranges)
- Hadith collections: `assets/hadith/{collection}/index.json` + book files

## Repository Pattern

- Repositories are plain Dart classes with static or instance methods
- They load JSON via `rootBundle.loadString()` and decode with `jsonDecode()`
- Return strongly-typed model objects (e.g., `ChapterMeta`, `HadithBook`, `Hadith`, `HadithChapter`)

## Models

- `ChapterMeta`: id, nameSimple, nameArabic, versesCount, revelationType, revelationOrder, startJuz, endJuz
  - `isMeccan` / `isMedinan` getters for filtering
- `HadithBook`: title, chapters, hadiths
- `Hadith`: id, idInBook, chapterId, bookId, arabic, english, narrator
- `QuranSearchHit` / `HadithSearchHit`: search result types in `lib/services/search_models.dart`
- `DailyVerse` / `DailyHadith`: daily content models in `lib/services/daily_content_service.dart`

## Quran Arabic JSON Fields

Each ayah in `KFGQPCQuranMushaf_smart_v8.json` has these fields:
- `id`: sequential ayah ID across entire Quran
- `jozz`: juz number (1-30)
- `sura_no`, `sura_name_en`, `sura_name_ar`: surah identifiers
- `page`: Mushaf page number
- `line_start`, `line_end`: line positions
- `aya_no`: ayah number within the surah
- `aya_text`: Uthmani Hafs Smart Unicode (for display, with full diacritics)
- `aya_text_emlaey`: simplified Arabic (for search only, never display this)

## Surah Metadata JSON

`assets/quran/surah_metadata.json` has per-surah entries:
- `id`: surah number (1-114)
- `revelationType`: "Meccan" or "Medinan"
- `revelationOrder`: chronological order (1-114)
- `startJuz` / `endJuz`: juz range

## Hadith JSON Structure

Each hadith book JSON has:
- `metadata`: title, author, introduction (Arabic + English)
- `chapters`: array of `HadithChapter` { id, bookId, arabic, english }
- `hadiths`: array of { id, idInBook, chapterId, bookId, arabic, english/narrator }

## Asset Paths

Use `AssetPaths` class (`lib/data/asset_paths.dart`) for constructing file paths. Do not hardcode asset paths.

## Settings Persistence

- `SharedPreferences` for theme mode and font zoom values
- `ThemeModeService` handles theme persistence
- `SettingsController` (ChangeNotifier) handles font zoom with `notifyListeners()`

## Daily Content

`DailyContentService` provides deterministic daily verse/hadith:
- Uses date-based seeding (same content all day, changes daily)
- Caches loaded content for the session
- Verse from random ayah across all 114 surahs
- Hadith from Nawawi 40 collection
